Step-by-step explanation
Create project directories
mkdir SYN
cd SYN
mkdir inputs outputs reports

Creates folders for the synthesis project.

Copy input files
cd inputs
cp -rf /home/moguthalama/pd_b3_b4/SYN/inputs/* .  [SYN inputs copied from this path] 
cd ../

Copies RTL, library, and SDC files into the project.

Start Synopsys DC Shell
which $SHELL
csh
source /home/tools/synopsys/cshrc_synopsys
dc_shell -output_log_file ./outputs/31_08_26.log  [-output_log_file --->command]

Loads the Synopsys environment and starts Design Compiler.


set search_path "/home/vgp4maneesh/pd_b3_b4/SYN/inputs" [verilog,sdc and librarys]
Specifies where DC should search for files.

Load technology library
set target_library ./inputs/saed32hvt_ss0p95v125c.db
set link_library ./inputs/saed32hvt_ss0p95v125c.db
target_library: Standard cell library used for synthesis. gates are choosen here in this file
link_library: Library used to resolve references.
Read RTL
analyze -format verilog ./inputs/mux.v -autoread -top mux_8_1

Reads the Verilog source of the 8:1 multiplexer.

Elaborate the design
elaborate mux_8_1

Builds the design hierarchy.

Read timing constraints
source ./inputs/mux.sdc

Loads the SDC file containing clock, input/output delays, etc.

Compile (Synthesis)
compile_ultra -no_autoungroup  [1--> optimization of time area power, stoping automatic ungrouping]

Maps the RTL to standard cells and optimizes for timing, area, and power.

Write gate-level netlist
write_file -format verilog -hierarchy -output ./outputs/mux.vg

Generates the synthesized Verilog netlist.
-hierarchy - top moule + sub moule code is preserved.without hierarchy only top module is preserved.

Write SDC
write_sdc ./outputs/mux.sdc

Saves the constraints after synthesis.

Generate reports
report_power
report_area
report_timing

Produces reports for:

Power
Area
Timing (setup/hold, slack)

